# Line-ending policy for ServerPackCreator.
#
# Why this file exists: the repo is uniformly LF, but nothing enforced it. A contributor with
# `core.autocrlf=true` (the Windows default in some setups) would commit CRLF shell scripts, and a CRLF
# `start.sh` fails at runtime with a "bad interpreter" error — in a *shipped* server pack. The templates
# under `serverpackcreator-api/src/main/resources/de/griefed/resources/server_files/` are the sharp edge:
# they are copied verbatim into every generated server pack, so their endings are user-facing.
#
# Rule of thumb: LF everywhere, CRLF only where Windows genuinely requires it.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Default: treat as text, store LF, check out LF on every platform.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
* text=auto eol=lf

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Must stay LF — a CRLF here breaks execution, not just the diff.
# Shell and fish scripts are run by an interpreter that chokes on carriage returns, and the SPC start
# templates become the scripts inside generated server packs.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.sh        text eol=lf
*.fish      text eol=lf
gradlew     text eol=lf

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Must be CRLF — Windows batch files. cmd.exe mis-parses LF-only .bat in some constructs (labels,
# multi-line blocks), so pin them explicitly. This covers Gradle's wrapper scripts *and*
# `default_template.bat`, which SPC turns into the `start.bat` shipped to Windows users.
# PowerShell is happy with LF, so .ps1 stays on the LF default.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.bat       text eol=crlf

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Tool-owned: left byte-for-byte alone so install4j can rewrite it without git reformatting it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
spc.install4j -text

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Binary — never touch. git's auto-detection already gets these right, but declaring them means a new
# fixture (the test jars, the icons, the sample modpack zip) can never be corrupted by normalisation.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.png       binary
*.jpg       binary
*.jpeg      binary
*.gif       binary
*.webp      binary
*.ico       binary
*.icns      binary
*.xcf       binary
*.jar       binary
*.zip       binary
*.gz        binary
*.exe       binary
*.dll       binary
*.so        binary
*.dylib     binary
*.ttf       binary
*.woff      binary
*.woff2     binary
*.pdf       binary
